            <ArticleTitle>Left heart pump-assisted beating heart coronary surgery in high-risk patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>159-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A simple technique of left ventricular assistance, offering the advantages of both cardiopulmonary bypass and off-pump revascularization, was adopted for high-risk patients. It was used in 56 patients with critical left main stenosis and occluded right coronary artery, severely reduced ejection fraction and/or unstable angina. All patients underwent complete and successful myocardial revascularization (3.4 grafts per patient). Weaning from the pump was uncomplicated, and none required conversion to full cardiopulmonary bypass.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
